-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party components distributed with the desktop installers
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The installers bundle a Python runtime and open-source libraries under their own
licenses, all of which allow redistribution in this form:

- Python (PSF License); FastAPI, Pydantic, PyYAML, MCP SDK, python-docx,
  openpyxl and others (MIT); Uvicorn, Starlette, HTTPX, pypdf, pywebview,
  lxml and others (BSD); Anthropic and OpenAI SDKs (Apache-2.0);
  cryptography (Apache-2.0 or BSD-3-Clause).
- PyInstaller bootloader (GPL-2.0 with the bootloader exception, which permits
  distributing the built application under any license).
- React, react-markdown and other web UI libraries (MIT, ISC).

Fonts (SIL Open Font License 1.1, https://openfontlicense.org):
- Chakra Petch. Copyright 2018 The Chakra Petch Project Authors
  (https://github.com/m4rc1e/Chakra-Petch).
- IBM Plex Sans and IBM Plex Mono. Copyright 2017-2019 IBM Corp.

Each component's license text is included in its package metadata. The full
list for a build can be produced with `uv pip list` (backend) and
`npm ls --omit=dev` (frontend).
